---
import { LuExternalLink } from "react-icons/lu"
---

<section class="flex flex-col gap-y-6 print:gap-y-1" id="about">
  <div class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold" id="about">About Me</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
    <div class="text-muted-foreground">
      I’m a Software Developer from Bangladesh who found my way into programming
      through the web. Building my first interactive pages with JavaScript made
      programming feel relatable, it was the first time I could see an idea turn
      into something real in the browser. That experience shaped how I approach
      software development today: I enjoy building things, understanding how
      they work, and continuously finding better ways to solve problems.
    </div>
    <div class="text-muted-foreground">
      After graduating, I joined Zventures LLC as a Frontend Intern and promoted
      to Frontend Developer within six months. Working on production SaaS
      applications taught me that good software is about much more than shipping
      features. It’s about writing maintainable and reusable code, thinking
      about performance, taking ownership of problems, and leaving the codebase
      in a better state for the next engineer.
    </div>
    <div class="text-muted-foreground">
      Outside of work, I enjoy learning by building. I spend time reading
      documentation, experimenting with personal projects, and exploring
      technologies beyond my day-to-day work. Recently, I’ve been diving deeper
      into backend development and AI-assisted workflows. I use AI to explore
      ideas, automate repetitive tasks, and understand unfamiliar technologies,
      but I still believe good software comes from thoughtful engineering
      decisions not blindly accepting generated code.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
